Demo_1.1A_JDBC_Database_Meta_data_JavaConfig
=========================================
Requirement: 
	From employee.csv file pump the Employee details to output.xml file.
	Using MySQL database as Job Repo/MetaData Database

Pre-requisite:
	Execute Employee.sql file script in MySQL database.

Observations:
 1) Open pom.xml file and observe the dependencies
 2) Observe SpringBatchConfig.java class for Spring batch configuration.
 3) Open UITester, Observe that AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(SpringBatchConfig.class) is used.  	
 4) Run the UITester main class, and Observe that output.xml created inside the xml folder	
 [Note: xml folder and output.xml file can be deleted. Both will be created on execution]
 
This demo is created to use Java configuration class instead of xml configuration file. [Alternative optionn]
 
Versions:
	Spring Batch : 4.3.4
	Spring 		      : 5.3.14
	MySQL 		  : 8.0.19
	
Reference Links :
	https://docs.spring.io/spring-batch/docs/4.3.4/reference/html/
